- id: '2098800030635171890'
  text: 'Gaussian Splats used to ignore the light. The scan stayed flat, even when
    a character or prop should have thrown a shadow across the floor.

    Get Splatbox here:

    https://t.co/luZuiIseRr


    Now the splat receives the shadow with near plane and bias. The tiles darken.
    The contact line sits on the reconstructed surface, not on a hidden plane in front
    of it.


    Near-plane control is the useful bit: you can push where that shadow begins, so
    it lifts off the object and lands on the splat like a real umbra — soft edge,
    right length, no black hole punched through the scan.


    #GaussianSplatting #3DGS #Unity3D #URP #RealtimeShadows #Relighting #SplatBox
    #ComputerGraphics #NovelViewSynthesis #GameDev'
