- id: '2099528129857441908'
  text: '🎉 A new Plinth release is here—capture, preview and share more of your world
    in 3D!


    🌍 Publish to SuperSplat

    Share completed Gaussian splats with a title, description and tags. A big thank-you
    to the @playcanvas team for SuperSplat!


    📸 Gaussian Quick Scan

    Automatically capture stationary objects and scenes as you move around them.


    ✨ On-device Gaussian previews

    Train and review a Gaussian preview on your device before uploading your project.


    📷 Camera improvements

    Improved camera startup and capture reliability, with ProRAW JPEG XL for supported
    photogrammetry and Gaussian capture workflows.


    🛠️ Photo review & dataset export

    See blur and exposure warnings more clearly, then export captured photos and metadata
    for use in other 3D tools.


    🔍 Improved Gaussian viewing

    Inspect splat counts and navigate results with improved loading and framing, plus
    fixes for the AR camera feed and iPad orientation.


    🗣️ Siri project search

    Open matching Plinth project results through Siri’s in-app search on iOS/iPadOS
    27.


    ♿ Accessibility

    Improved VoiceOver controls for photo review and Gaussian previews, with layouts
    that adapt to larger text.


    🔄 More reliable workflows

    Improvements to sign-in, file imports, upload recovery, project deletion and Live
    Activities.


    Quick Scan and on-device Gaussian previews require iOS/iPadOS 27 and Professional
    access. Quick Scan also requires LiDAR.


    Thank you to everyone capturing, testing and sharing with Plinth. What will you
    scan—and share—next? 💛


    #Plinth #SuperSplat #GaussianSplatting #3DScanning #Photogrammetry'
