- id: '2098155617001382230'
  text: "Up to 8K textures. On Gaussian splats with no training. That looks like a\
    \ 4D character.\n https://t.co/luZuiIsMGZ\nThat’s because Gaussian splats normally\
    \ bake appearance. Each splat stores a single color.\n\nEach splat now keeps the\
    \ original mesh UVs. While it renders, it reads the 8K map live across its surface\
    \ — pores, fabric weave, stitching, leather grain.\n \nThe high-res texture stays\
    \ a real texture, not a smeared average. Then the skeleton takes over. Bones skin\
    \ the splats in real time, so the character can walk, turn, and perform — with\
    \ the 8K detail still on the body.\n\nWhat you actually get:\n\n- Close-ups that\
    \ still look like a real 4D character\n- 8K albedo that survives conversion\n\
    - A splat figure that animates, not a frozen scan\n\nRigged 8K splat characters,\
    \ coming for Splat Rigger on SplatBox.\n#GaussianSplatting #SplatBox #SplatRigger\
    \ #3DGS #SOTA #Unity #VolumetricRendering"
